1
00:00:03,630 --> 00:00:04,920
This is an easy one.

2
00:00:04,920 --> 00:00:06,560
You love this guy.

3
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:07,830
Me.

4
00:00:09,340 --> 00:00:12,890
Come on. He's an underappreciated genius.

5
00:00:12,890 --> 00:00:14,880
Still think it's me.

6
00:00:15,640 --> 00:00:16,920
It's not you.

7
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:19,600
Now think, there's a car named after him.

8
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:20,920
Of course there is.

9
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:24,460
The Mini Cooper 'cause it's me.

10
00:00:25,310 --> 00:00:27,010
How about this:

11
00:00:27,010 --> 00:00:29,150
he's a poor man's Sheldon Cooper.

12
00:00:29,150 --> 00:00:30,700
Oh, Tesla.

13
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:34,600
- How'd it go? - Oh, not fun.

14
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:37,260
The doctor shoved a camera up into my sinuses.

15
00:00:37,260 --> 00:00:38,130
Yeah, I watched.

16
00:00:38,130 --> 00:00:42,200
It was like the scary boat tunnel in Willy Wonka.

17
00:00:42,870 --> 00:00:44,230
- Did they figure out what's wrong? - Yeah.

18
00:00:44,230 --> 00:00:45,870
It's a deviated septum.

19
00:00:45,870 --> 00:00:47,260
The surgery to correct it is simple.

20
00:00:47,260 --> 00:00:48,440
He's gonna do it next week.

21
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:50,250
Why would you have surgery?

22
00:00:50,250 --> 00:00:51,970
Because I can't breathe.

23
00:00:51,970 --> 00:00:54,290
I snore, I get sinus infections...

24
00:00:54,290 --> 00:00:57,130
Yeah, back off, he's all mine.

25
00:00:57,130 --> 00:00:59,190
But you don't have a life-threatening condition.

26
00:00:59,190 --> 00:01:01,070
Why would you take the risk of surgery?

27
00:01:01,070 --> 00:01:02,880
Sheldon, it's a routine procedure.

28
00:01:02,880 --> 00:01:04,890
I've heard you complain about his snoring.

29
00:01:04,890 --> 00:01:07,180
We... Yes, for the first five or six years,

30
00:01:07,180 --> 00:01:09,230
but I've gotten used to it.

31
00:01:09,230 --> 00:01:11,040
It helps me sleep.

32
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:14,930
He's like my mucus-powered white noise machine.

33
00:01:15,080 --> 00:01:17,240
Sheldon, I'm gonna get the surgery, it's no big deal.

34
00:01:17,240 --> 00:01:18,150
End of story.

35
00:01:18,150 --> 00:01:20,030
Very well. I'm done talking about it.

36
00:01:20,030 --> 00:01:20,620
Thank you.

37
00:01:20,620 --> 00:01:22,180
 I believe it was your turn in the game.

38
00:01:22,180 --> 00:01:23,260
Okay.

39
00:01:24,950 --> 00:01:26,210
Let's see...

40
00:01:26,210 --> 00:01:28,820
Oh, this person is most famous

41
00:01:28,820 --> 00:01:32,840
for never having gotten his nose mutilated with elective surgery

42
00:01:32,850 --> 00:01:35,690
and never living the rest of his life in the shadows

43
00:01:35,690 --> 00:01:38,370
as a hideous, disfigured freak.

44
00:01:39,070 --> 00:01:40,830
I think you could give a better clue.

45
00:01:40,830 --> 00:01:41,920
I don't.

46
00:01:42,380 --> 00:01:45,050
I'm not even sure if that's a person or a typo.

47
00:02:25,560 --> 00:02:27,790
Okay, why?

48
00:02:28,530 --> 00:02:30,750
I'm listening to you snore.

49
00:02:31,160 --> 00:02:33,820
I'm wondering how I'll ever sleep without it.

50
00:02:34,860 --> 00:02:36,260
If it helps you sleep,

51
00:02:36,260 --> 00:02:38,310
then why are you sitting here staring at me

52
00:02:38,310 --> 00:02:41,500
like the albino boogeyman?

53
00:02:42,190 --> 00:02:43,880
Really, Leonard-- insults?

54
00:02:43,880 --> 00:02:45,560
After I spent two hours in your closet,

55
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:47,670
waiting for you to fall asleep?

56
00:02:50,210 --> 00:02:51,880
What's your problem?

57
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:55,510
If the surgery is successful, the snoring is gone.

58
00:02:55,510 --> 00:02:58,270
And if you die during surgery...

59
00:02:59,120 --> 00:03:01,330
...the snoring is gone.

60
00:03:02,530 --> 00:03:05,790
It sounds like either way, I finally get some rest.

61
00:03:06,330 --> 00:03:07,720
I have to be honest with you Leonard,

62
00:03:07,720 --> 00:03:09,470
I'm truly worried.

63
00:03:09,470 --> 00:03:12,180
I-I told you, there's nothing to worry about.

64
00:03:12,180 --> 00:03:13,880
Well, I've been doing some research

65
00:03:13,880 --> 00:03:16,470
and I've learned that one in 700,000 people

66
00:03:16,470 --> 00:03:18,980
die from general anesthesia.

67
00:03:18,980 --> 00:03:21,330
Buddy, w... Do you realize that that also means

68
00:03:21,330 --> 00:03:26,390
699,999 people don't die?

69
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:29,580
I suppose that's true.

70
00:03:30,770 --> 00:03:34,100
You're such a glass half-full kind of guy.

71
00:03:35,260 --> 00:03:37,220
I'm going to miss that.

72
00:03:40,380 --> 00:03:43,300
Oh, so, my, uh, parents' 40th anniversary's coming up

73
00:03:43,300 --> 00:03:45,850
and I can't think of a thing to get them.

74
00:03:45,850 --> 00:03:47,170
Damn, can you imagine

75
00:03:47,170 --> 00:03:50,720
being married to someone for 40 years?

76
00:03:53,660 --> 00:03:55,580
Not anymore.

77
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:02,430
Anyway, any ideas on a gift?

78
00:04:02,430 --> 00:04:04,540
Well, what are some of the things they like?

79
00:04:04,850 --> 00:04:07,130
They used to like going to the Mumbai Symphony,

80
00:04:07,130 --> 00:04:09,360
but last year my mom thought they were phoning it in.

81
00:04:09,360 --> 00:04:10,620
Then my dad said based on their love life,

82
00:04:10,620 --> 00:04:13,620
she should know about phoning it in.

83
00:04:14,870 --> 00:04:16,910
- He said that to her? - Well, they weren't speaking at the time,

84
00:04:16,910 --> 00:04:19,230
so he had a servant say it to her.

85
00:04:19,710 --> 00:04:22,020
Oh, maybe I could make a gift for them.

86
00:04:22,020 --> 00:04:25,980
I know how much you guys love the coasters I made for you.

87
00:04:28,240 --> 00:04:30,570
They're yours in the divorce.

88
00:04:34,990 --> 00:04:36,610
Hey. What're you working on?

89
00:04:36,610 --> 00:04:39,290
Remember when I said if you went through with your surgery,

90
00:04:39,290 --> 00:04:42,210
there was a one-in-700,000 chance of dying?

91
00:04:42,970 --> 00:04:44,020
Yeah...?

92
00:04:44,020 --> 00:04:46,170
Well, I've been crunching the numbers,

93
00:04:46,170 --> 00:04:49,240
and so far, I've gotten your probability of death

94
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:53,420
all the way to a sphincter-tightening one in 300.

95
00:04:55,580 --> 00:04:56,540
Great timing.

96
00:04:56,540 --> 00:04:59,230
My "Check sphincter" light just went on.

97
00:05:00,130 --> 00:05:02,570
Leonard, what if you have an allergic reaction

98
00:05:02,570 --> 00:05:04,110
to the surgeon's latex gloves?

99
00:05:04,110 --> 00:05:05,800
I'm not allergic to latex.

100
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:07,220
Well, then why don't you wear the rubber gloves

101
00:05:07,220 --> 00:05:08,770
I bought for you to do the dishes?

102
00:05:08,770 --> 00:05:12,110
For the same reason I don't wear the apron or the hair net.

103
00:05:12,760 --> 00:05:15,300
Fine. What about epilepsy?

104
00:05:15,300 --> 00:05:16,930
I don't have epilepsy, either.

105
00:05:16,930 --> 00:05:19,050
You don't, but the surgeon might, hmm?

106
00:05:19,990 --> 00:05:23,080
And your carotid artery is just one shaky scalpel away

107
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:25,850
from becoming the dancing fountain at Disneyland.

108
00:05:26,700 --> 00:05:29,890
Sheldon, do you realize that driving is riskier than surgery?

109
00:05:29,890 --> 00:05:33,070
I do. I have the drive to the hospital right here.

110
00:05:33,730 --> 00:05:34,970
That is if you make it to the car

111
00:05:34,970 --> 00:05:37,200
without falling down the stairs.

112
00:05:37,200 --> 00:05:40,430
And don't expect me to carry you, I do that enough in life.

113
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:43,340
Buddy, I-I get that you're worried about me

114
00:05:43,340 --> 00:05:46,060
and I-I appreciate that, but I'm not going to die.

115
00:05:46,060 --> 00:05:47,760
You don't know that.

116
00:05:47,760 --> 00:05:51,340
I do know that it won't be from an asteroid strike.

117
00:05:52,630 --> 00:05:54,190
You know who else said that?

118
00:05:54,190 --> 00:05:55,600
Every cocky T. Rex currently

119
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:58,560
swimming around in the gas tank of your car.

120
00:05:59,150 --> 00:06:00,810
I-If there was an asteroid strike,

121
00:06:00,810 --> 00:06:02,150
wouldn't you die, too?

122
00:06:02,150 --> 00:06:03,760
I don't know-- I'm smart and scrappy,

123
00:06:03,760 --> 00:06:05,760
I think I'd find a way.

124
00:06:08,220 --> 00:06:10,350
Tell you what-- the surgery's not for a week,

125
00:06:10,350 --> 00:06:11,260
I'll think about it.

126
00:06:11,260 --> 00:06:12,690
Thank you.

127
00:06:12,690 --> 00:06:14,120
And while you're thinking about it,

128
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:17,060
if you have the surgery in Nicaragua during monsoon season,

129
00:06:17,060 --> 00:06:19,650
I can practically guarantee your death.

130
00:06:24,950 --> 00:06:26,680
Yes. Okay.

131
00:06:27,310 --> 00:06:28,980
I-I understand.

132
00:06:29,360 --> 00:06:30,120
Of course, yes.

133
00:06:30,120 --> 00:06:31,320
I'll call you tomorrow.

134
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:32,810
Bye.

135
00:06:33,890 --> 00:06:37,240
So I found this fencing school in Burbank

136
00:06:37,240 --> 00:06:40,240
that has a Jedi class.

137
00:06:41,520 --> 00:06:43,200
And if you're cool being the only adults there,

138
00:06:43,200 --> 00:06:44,950
they said they are.

139
00:06:46,510 --> 00:06:48,200
Dude, my parents just split up.

140
00:06:48,200 --> 00:06:49,090
What?!

141
00:06:49,090 --> 00:06:50,990
Uh, that was my dad on the phone.

142
00:06:50,990 --> 00:06:52,670
He moved out.

143
00:06:52,910 --> 00:06:56,580
Oh, my God, I... I'm sorry.

144
00:06:56,580 --> 00:06:58,720
I mean, if you're not up to it, we don't have to go out,

145
00:06:58,720 --> 00:07:00,150
we can just hang here.

146
00:07:00,150 --> 00:07:01,510
No, it's fine.

147
00:07:01,510 --> 00:07:02,940
It's not that big a deal.

148
00:07:02,940 --> 00:07:05,100
As long as they're happy, I'm happy.

149
00:07:05,100 --> 00:07:07,540
And when I get to see them for the holidays,

150
00:07:07,540 --> 00:07:09,490
I'll get to celebrate Diwali twice--

151
00:07:09,490 --> 00:07:11,480
one at each house.

152
00:07:13,370 --> 00:07:15,700
That's double the Diwali.

153
00:07:16,830 --> 00:07:18,100
You sure you're okay?

154
00:07:18,100 --> 00:07:18,860
I'm okay.

155
00:07:18,860 --> 00:07:19,860
You don't look okay.

156
00:07:19,860 --> 00:07:23,270
How can I be okay? I come from a broken home.

157
00:07:25,850 --> 00:07:28,270
The doctor said I should be out of surgery by 10:00.

158
00:07:28,270 --> 00:07:29,440
Okay.

159
00:07:29,440 --> 00:07:31,080
And Sheldon really believes

160
00:07:31,080 --> 00:07:33,240
we're at a public swimming pool?

161
00:07:34,860 --> 00:07:36,320
He was so busy figuring out

162
00:07:36,320 --> 00:07:38,520
how many parts per million of urine we'd be floating around in,

163
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:40,630
he didn't even question it.

164
00:07:41,570 --> 00:07:44,260
18 parts per million.

165
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:47,870
And he's still doing it.

166
00:07:47,870 --> 00:07:50,600
Don't worry about that. I'm happy to take you to work.

167
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:51,860
Well, thank you.

168
00:07:51,860 --> 00:07:55,770
And Leonard never lets me have French toast sticks in the car.

169
00:07:55,950 --> 00:07:57,910
I can't have syrupy fingers,

170
00:07:57,910 --> 00:08:01,120
but he can do the backstroke in a toilet bowl.

171
00:08:02,660 --> 00:08:04,940
It's nice they're getting exercise.

172
00:08:05,530 --> 00:08:07,900
Although now that I think about it,

173
00:08:07,900 --> 00:08:09,820
Leonard would never go swimming in public

174
00:08:09,820 --> 00:08:12,280
without his swim shirt.

175
00:08:13,340 --> 00:08:14,940
I'm sure he brought it.

176
00:08:14,940 --> 00:08:17,040
No, but last year, at Magic Mountain,

177
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:18,440
he got such a bad sunburn,

178
00:08:18,440 --> 00:08:20,960
we had to cut him out of it.

179
00:08:22,200 --> 00:08:24,550
He probably got a new one. Finish your breakfast.

180
00:08:24,550 --> 00:08:26,350
Look, there's an entire section of my dashboard

181
00:08:26,350 --> 00:08:28,400
that doesn't have any syrup on it.

182
00:08:29,630 --> 00:08:32,500
You're acting odd. Why?

183
00:08:32,820 --> 00:08:35,450
I'm odd all the time, everyone knows that.

184
00:08:35,450 --> 00:08:37,660
Just last night, I tried to see how many fava beans

185
00:08:37,660 --> 00:08:39,860
I could fit in my mouth.

186
00:08:40,910 --> 00:08:42,370
Tell me the truth.

187
00:08:42,370 --> 00:08:43,830
28.

188
00:08:44,280 --> 00:08:46,270
- Come on. - Fifty-six.

189
00:08:47,930 --> 00:08:49,000
Amy!

190
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:51,090
What's going on?

191
00:08:51,090 --> 00:08:52,390
All right.

192
00:08:53,350 --> 00:08:55,210
Don't get upset, but...

193
00:08:55,600 --> 00:08:57,840
an earlier appointment opened up for Leonard

194
00:08:57,840 --> 00:09:01,280
and he's getting the surgery right now.

195
00:09:05,020 --> 00:09:06,640
I see.

196
00:09:12,370 --> 00:09:13,960
Take me to Leonard.

197
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:15,910
Just go to work, he'll be fine.

198
00:09:15,910 --> 00:09:17,810
Amy, he's my best friend,

199
00:09:17,810 --> 00:09:20,630
and if you don't take me, I'm going there anyway.

200
00:09:21,190 --> 00:09:22,520
Fine.

201
00:09:23,550 --> 00:09:25,900
It's sweet that you care about him so much.

202
00:09:25,900 --> 00:09:26,920
I do.

203
00:09:27,530 --> 00:09:28,820
And I wouldn't be able to forgive myself,

204
00:09:28,820 --> 00:09:30,190
if something happened to him

205
00:09:30,190 --> 00:09:33,810
and I wasn't at his bedside to say, "I told you so."

206
00:09:46,890 --> 00:09:47,940
Hello.

207
00:09:47,940 --> 00:09:49,360
We had a really nice swim.

208
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:50,570
Oh, stop it.

209
00:09:52,290 --> 00:09:54,290
I assume this medical center's already treated

210
00:09:54,290 --> 00:09:58,490
the burns on your bottom from the recent pants fire.

211
00:09:59,270 --> 00:10:00,990
'Cause I'm a liar, liar?

212
00:10:00,990 --> 00:10:03,270
That's for the fire marshal to determine.

213
00:10:04,670 --> 00:10:05,860
You had to tell him?

214
00:10:05,860 --> 00:10:07,670
He wore me down.

215
00:10:07,670 --> 00:10:08,820
And I was distracted.

216
00:10:08,820 --> 00:10:11,540
He has on extra baby powder today.

217
00:10:12,830 --> 00:10:13,820
Is he okay?

218
00:10:13,820 --> 00:10:15,320
He's still in surgery.

219
00:10:16,610 --> 00:10:17,960
Very well.

220
00:10:17,960 --> 00:10:20,220
He's gonna be all right.

221
00:10:20,800 --> 00:10:22,620
That is sticky.

222
00:10:24,950 --> 00:10:27,740
Come on, let's talk about something other than the surgery.

223
00:10:27,740 --> 00:10:29,100
That's a good idea.

224
00:10:29,530 --> 00:10:33,900
Penny, did you and Leonard ever discuss funeral arrangements?

225
00:10:35,060 --> 00:10:38,170
I think she meant something a little happier.

226
00:10:38,860 --> 00:10:41,860
I suppose we could try to make it a celebration,

227
00:10:41,860 --> 00:10:44,250
but he died so young.

228
00:10:47,850 --> 00:10:49,500
- Knock, knock. Hi. - Hey.

229
00:10:49,500 --> 00:10:51,110
What brings you by?

230
00:10:52,630 --> 00:10:55,260
muffin much.

231
00:10:56,600 --> 00:10:58,540
Told you-- not funny.

232
00:10:59,220 --> 00:11:00,410
He's just not laughing

233
00:11:00,410 --> 00:11:04,780
because he's feeling... blue berry.

234
00:11:06,230 --> 00:11:07,620
Tough crowd.

235
00:11:09,940 --> 00:11:12,480
I'm sorry. This is very sweet. Thanks.

236
00:11:12,480 --> 00:11:13,710
So, how you doing?

237
00:11:13,710 --> 00:11:15,410
Better. I guess the news just

238
00:11:15,410 --> 00:11:17,480
hit me a lot harder than I expected.

239
00:11:17,480 --> 00:11:18,570
Well, of course.

240
00:11:18,570 --> 00:11:21,350
I would be devastated if my parents split up.

241
00:11:21,350 --> 00:11:24,430
Why? Your father barely speaks to your mother.

242
00:11:24,430 --> 00:11:25,880
Well, at least he stuck around,

243
00:11:25,880 --> 00:11:28,270
not like your dad, who just took off.

244
00:11:28,270 --> 00:11:31,010
As you can see, we're here to cheer you up.

245
00:11:32,390 --> 00:11:33,530
Sorry, Raj.

246
00:11:33,530 --> 00:11:36,050
Do you have any sense of what happened with your folks?

247
00:11:36,050 --> 00:11:39,420
I think, over time, they started to resent each other,

248
00:11:39,420 --> 00:11:41,640
and instead of talking about the things that bothered them,

249
00:11:41,640 --> 00:11:42,990
they kept it bottled up,

250
00:11:42,990 --> 00:11:44,960
and the hate just grew.

251
00:11:44,960 --> 00:11:47,750
It's a shame they spent all that time unhappy.

252
00:11:48,360 --> 00:11:49,810
But sometimes,

253
00:11:49,810 --> 00:11:52,750
there's muffin you can do about it.

254
00:11:54,850 --> 00:11:56,990
You get it, right?

255
00:12:00,830 --> 00:12:02,430
Oh, it's nice you got him that.

256
00:12:02,430 --> 00:12:04,380
Oh, this isn't for Leonard, no.

257
00:12:04,380 --> 00:12:06,480
Amy bought it for me.

258
00:12:09,020 --> 00:12:11,990
Stubbed his toe on the revolving door on the way in.

259
00:12:11,990 --> 00:12:14,740
You know those confounded things make me dizzy.

260
00:12:14,740 --> 00:12:17,640
Who told you to keep going around?

261
00:12:17,970 --> 00:12:19,720
There was a large plant in the lobby.

262
00:12:19,720 --> 00:12:22,220
It kept looking like the outside.

263
00:12:23,330 --> 00:12:24,580
Okay, listen, when Leonard comes out,

264
00:12:24,580 --> 00:12:25,550
he is not gonna feel great,

265
00:12:25,550 --> 00:12:27,640
so, please don't give him a hard time.

266
00:12:27,640 --> 00:12:29,280
Penny has a good point.

267
00:12:29,280 --> 00:12:31,280
This is like the man in the supermarket

268
00:12:31,280 --> 00:12:32,830
with the goiter on his neck.

269
00:12:32,830 --> 00:12:35,850
Whatever you're thinking, just keep it to yourself.

270
00:12:36,750 --> 00:12:39,150
It was like a grapefruit.

271
00:12:39,820 --> 00:12:41,250
And I'm sure he knew that

272
00:12:41,250 --> 00:12:44,290
before you held a grapefruit up next to it.

273
00:12:44,850 --> 00:12:46,660
Well, I'm not making any promises.

274
00:12:46,660 --> 00:12:49,460
Not only did Leonard take what I feel is an unnecessary risk,

275
00:12:49,460 --> 00:12:50,550
he deceived me.

276
00:12:50,550 --> 00:12:51,780
Okay, the reason he deceived you is

277
00:12:51,780 --> 00:12:53,420
you were being a pain in the ass.

278
00:12:53,420 --> 00:12:55,570
The reason I was being a pain in the B is

279
00:12:55,570 --> 00:12:57,870
because I was worried about him, and no one else was.

280
00:12:57,870 --> 00:12:59,610
Really? You won't even say "A"?

281
00:12:59,610 --> 00:13:01,930
You bet your sweet B I won't.

282
00:13:02,590 --> 00:13:04,090
Obviously, I care about Leonard.

283
00:13:04,090 --> 00:13:05,920
I'm gonna spend the rest of my life with him.

284
00:13:05,920 --> 00:13:08,010
And I'm not?

285
00:13:11,230 --> 00:13:12,380
It's an earthquake.

286
00:13:12,380 --> 00:13:13,650
I knew it.

287
00:13:13,650 --> 00:13:15,290
Sheldon, it was just a little tremor.

288
00:13:15,290 --> 00:13:18,050
A little tremor that turns routine sinus surgery

289
00:13:18,050 --> 00:13:20,290
into a frontal lobotomy.

290
00:13:23,900 --> 00:13:25,920
Oh, I don't care for this at all.

291
00:13:25,920 --> 00:13:28,020
Oh, I need to see he's okay.

292
00:13:28,020 --> 00:13:29,900
Sheldon, you can't go back there.

293
00:13:29,900 --> 00:13:31,400
Try and stop me!

294
00:13:34,150 --> 00:13:35,550
Are you okay?

295
00:13:35,550 --> 00:13:38,060
Why didn't you stop me?!

296
00:13:41,140 --> 00:13:42,630
Can I tell you something?

297
00:13:42,980 --> 00:13:44,880
This whole thing with Raj's parents

298
00:13:44,880 --> 00:13:47,420
just got me a little worried about us.

299
00:13:47,420 --> 00:13:49,880
What are you talking about? We're fine.

300
00:13:49,880 --> 00:13:53,360
And Raj's parents probably split up because of Raj.

301
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:55,650
What?!

302
00:13:55,650 --> 00:13:58,580
They always say the children aren't to blame, but...

303
00:13:59,010 --> 00:14:00,430
Come on.

304
00:14:04,190 --> 00:14:05,860
I'm not joking, Howie.

305
00:14:05,860 --> 00:14:07,430
You heard what he said about his parents.

306
00:14:07,430 --> 00:14:09,860
It was the little things they kept bottled up.

307
00:14:09,860 --> 00:14:12,090
I don't want that to happen to us.

308
00:14:12,090 --> 00:14:14,120
How can I convince you it won't?

309
00:14:14,120 --> 00:14:17,700
Well, is there anything about me you're keeping inside?

310
00:14:18,660 --> 00:14:19,600
I'm not answering that.

311
00:14:19,600 --> 00:14:20,830
It's a trap.

312
00:14:24,390 --> 00:14:26,810
So there are things you don't like.

313
00:14:26,810 --> 00:14:29,330
And here I am in the trap.

314
00:14:31,440 --> 00:14:32,510
You just keep talking.

315
00:14:32,510 --> 00:14:34,640
I'm gonna chew my leg off.

316
00:14:35,690 --> 00:14:37,210
Just tell me one thing that bothers you,

317
00:14:37,210 --> 00:14:39,250
and I promise I won't get mad.

318
00:14:39,250 --> 00:14:41,920
Okay. The truth is...

319
00:14:41,920 --> 00:14:44,440
sometimes... you're too...

320
00:14:44,440 --> 00:14:46,270
beautiful.

321
00:14:48,670 --> 00:14:50,380
Howie, be serious.

322
00:14:50,380 --> 00:14:52,090
Okay, okay.

323
00:14:52,090 --> 00:14:54,940
I really don't like

324
00:14:54,940 --> 00:14:57,140
how your wings poke me when we sleep

325
00:14:57,140 --> 00:14:59,030
'cause you're an angel.

326
00:15:01,840 --> 00:15:03,880
Okay, fine, maybe it was a bad idea.

327
00:15:03,880 --> 00:15:05,680
I just don't think the secret to a happy marriage

328
00:15:05,680 --> 00:15:08,760
is going out of our way to criticize each other.

329
00:15:08,760 --> 00:15:12,910
Although, there are ways to improve our communication.

330
00:15:12,910 --> 00:15:15,530
One thing I learned when I was in couples therapy was...

331
00:15:15,530 --> 00:15:17,110
Who were you in couples therapy with?

332
00:15:17,110 --> 00:15:18,570
Not important.

333
00:15:20,560 --> 00:15:21,420
Was it your mom?

334
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:22,680
Not important.

335
00:15:23,870 --> 00:15:25,160
It was your mom.

336
00:15:26,820 --> 00:15:29,000
Anyway, the therapist had us tell each other

337
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:31,920
what we loved about one another.

338
00:15:31,920 --> 00:15:33,650
Oh, that's so sweet!

339
00:15:33,650 --> 00:15:35,010
I want to do that.

340
00:15:35,010 --> 00:15:36,230
All right.

341
00:15:37,110 --> 00:15:38,460
Okay, um...

342
00:15:38,460 --> 00:15:41,480
I love that you make me laugh.

343
00:15:41,480 --> 00:15:42,810
Thank you.

344
00:15:42,810 --> 00:15:47,920
And I love that you're strong and independent.

345
00:15:47,920 --> 00:15:50,950
And yet, I still love when you hold a door for me.

346
00:15:50,950 --> 00:15:54,830
I love that I'm kind of a slob around here, and...

347
00:15:54,830 --> 00:15:57,180
you're okay with that.

348
00:16:00,780 --> 00:16:02,290
Uh-huh.

349
00:16:03,860 --> 00:16:06,080
And I love that I work and do all the cleaning,

350
00:16:06,080 --> 00:16:08,310
and you're okay with that.

351
00:16:10,070 --> 00:16:11,000
See, I am.

352
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:12,890
Isn't this great?

353
00:16:16,230 --> 00:16:17,450
Come on, smile.

354
00:16:17,450 --> 00:16:19,970
This is gonna be my Christmas card.

355
00:16:24,640 --> 00:16:26,640
You know this is all your fault.

356
00:16:27,690 --> 00:16:29,490
How is it my fault?

357
00:16:31,360 --> 00:16:33,740
I told you not to get the surgery.

358
00:16:33,740 --> 00:16:37,100
Okay, first of all, the surgery was a success,

359
00:16:37,100 --> 00:16:39,680
and secondly, I didn't even want you there.

360
00:16:41,530 --> 00:16:42,640
I don't know which hurts worse--

361
00:16:42,640 --> 00:16:44,860
my nose or my heart.

362
00:16:46,100 --> 00:16:47,780
Well, I'm done speaking to you.

363
00:16:47,780 --> 00:16:48,750
Don't be like that.

364
00:16:48,750 --> 00:16:50,390
You two need to talk this out.

365
00:16:50,390 --> 00:16:53,350
Yeah, 'cause you sound really funny.

366
00:16:55,620 --> 00:16:58,140
Sheldon, I'm sorry I didn't tell you about the surgery,

367
00:16:58,140 --> 00:17:00,110
but you were worried about nothing.

368
00:17:00,110 --> 00:17:02,130
Oh, you're hardly out of the woods, no.

369
00:17:02,130 --> 00:17:05,390
You still run the risk of infection, a blood clot,

370
00:17:05,390 --> 00:17:07,420
the possibility that an inattentive surgeon

371
00:17:07,420 --> 00:17:10,650
let a barn spider lay eggs in your nose.

372
00:17:12,150 --> 00:17:15,360
The minute you sneeze web, I'm moving out.

373
00:17:15,750 --> 00:17:17,480
I never thought I'd say these words,

374
00:17:17,480 --> 00:17:20,150
but come on, nose spider!

375
00:17:21,100 --> 00:17:22,280
Who are you kidding?

376
00:17:22,280 --> 00:17:24,110
You were so panicked Leonard was gonna die,

377
00:17:24,110 --> 00:17:25,330
you'll never leave him.

378
00:17:25,330 --> 00:17:27,110
Sheldon will move out eventually.

379
00:17:27,110 --> 00:17:29,910
Yeah, once he figures out how to work a door.

380
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:34,840
I was not panicked, and I am not overly attached to Leonard.

381
00:17:34,840 --> 00:17:36,930
You were so worried that you smashed your face

382
00:17:36,930 --> 00:17:38,080
trying to check on me.

383
00:17:38,080 --> 00:17:40,530
You love me.

384
00:17:41,620 --> 00:17:43,180
Yeah. Tell me those aren't the words of a man

385
00:17:43,180 --> 00:17:46,100
with a spider eating its way through his brain.

386
00:17:46,770 --> 00:17:48,370
Amy, you're a neuroscientist.

387
00:17:48,370 --> 00:17:51,320
Crack his skull open, spray some Raid in there.

388
00:17:54,030 --> 00:17:56,500
I love that you take pride in your looks,

389
00:17:56,500 --> 00:17:57,860
even when I have to pee in the morning,

390
00:17:57,860 --> 00:18:01,260
and you're in there spending an hour on your hair.

391
00:18:01,900 --> 00:18:06,270
I love that you're too good to pee in the kitchen sink.

392
00:18:06,760 --> 00:18:08,850
I love that you have the confidence to speak,

393
00:18:08,850 --> 00:18:11,790
even without giving it an ounce of thought.

394
00:18:13,450 --> 00:18:15,580
And I love how your hair is always on the soap.

395
00:18:15,580 --> 00:18:18,510
It's like washing myself with a hamster.

396
00:18:20,210 --> 00:18:23,680
Hey, guys. Sorry I am so late.

397
00:18:23,680 --> 00:18:25,870
I was on the phone with my mother.

398
00:18:25,870 --> 00:18:27,110
Oh, how is she?

399
00:18:27,110 --> 00:18:28,230
Pretty good.

400
00:18:28,230 --> 00:18:30,330
She bought the book Eat, Pray, Love

401
00:18:30,330 --> 00:18:33,310
and used it to set my father's Mercedes on fire.

402
00:18:35,560 --> 00:18:38,210
So, what's up with you guys?

403
00:18:38,980 --> 00:18:41,430
We're just saying all the things we love about each other.

404
00:18:41,430 --> 00:18:44,210
Oh, like you and I did at couples therapy.

405
00:18:53,560 --> 00:18:54,700
Ooh, what'd you get?

406
00:18:54,700 --> 00:18:57,530
Oh, I ordered it before your surgery.

407
00:18:57,530 --> 00:19:00,690
It's the urn I was going to put you in.

408
00:19:02,150 --> 00:19:03,650
Okay, that's morbid.

409
00:19:03,650 --> 00:19:04,780
Send it back.

410
00:19:04,780 --> 00:19:08,310
I can't send it back-- I had it engraved.

411
00:19:09,250 --> 00:19:12,370
"Here lie the ashes of Leonard Hofstadter.

412
00:19:12,370 --> 00:19:16,170
He thought he was right, but his roommate knew better."

413
00:19:18,710 --> 00:19:20,160
That's funny.

414
00:19:20,610 --> 00:19:23,000
Boy, I'm gonna miss these painkillers.

415
00:19:23,830 --> 00:19:26,230
Hey, why did you get two?

416
00:19:26,230 --> 00:19:28,960
- "I'm with stupid." - Oh, that one's mine.

